{"id": "tea:yogabindu:31", "source": "src:yogabindu", "location": {"ref": "31", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Adhyātma, cultivation (bhāvanā), meditation, equanimity (samatā) and the ending of mental activity (vṛttisaṃkṣaya) — this yoga, because it joins [the soul] to liberation, is better in each successive stage.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:adhyatma", "trm:bhavana", "trm:dhyana", "trm:samata", "trm:vrttisanksaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:haribhadra-five-yogas"], "paths": ["pth:yogabindu-five-yogas"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogabindu:anusthana", "source": "src:yogabindu", "location": {"ref": "anusthana", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Religious performance is of five kinds: 'poison' (done for this-worldly gain), 'venom' (for heavenly reward), mechanical non-performance, performance that is a cause [of the true], and 'nectar' (done with right understanding and longing for liberation); the first three are to be avoided.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-anusthanas"], "obstacles": ["obs:visa-gara-anusthana"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Section-level ref.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogabindu:caramavarta", "source": "src:yogabindu", "location": {"ref": "caramavarta", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Only a soul in its last cycle of worldly existence (caramāvarta), who no longer binds karma of the most intense kind (apunarbandhaka), is fit for yoga; for others the teaching does not take hold.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:caramavarta", "trm:apunarbandhaka"], "concepts": ["cpt:apunarbandhaka-caramavarta"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Section-level ref.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogabindu:purvaseva", "source": "src:yogabindu", "location": {"ref": "purvaseva", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Before yoga come the preliminaries (pūrvasevā): worship of teachers and gods, good conduct, austerity, and non-aversion to liberation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "action"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:purvaseva"], "concepts": ["cpt:apunarbandhaka-caramavarta"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Section-level ref.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogabindu:vrttisanksaya", "source": "src:yogabindu", "location": {"ref": "vrttisanksaya", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "In the ending of mental activity the soul's activities born of the body and mind cease at their root; from it come omniscience and liberation.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:vrttisanksaya", "trm:kevala-jnana"], "concepts": ["cpt:haribhadra-five-yogas"], "paths": ["pth:yogabindu-five-yogas"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
